## Decisions Made

- **Ownership follows payment truth**: `isOwned` semantics unchanged; instead, removal makes not-owned legitimate by actually reverting the payment first. Wallet refunds go through the finance ledger (single source of balance), external rails are record-only.
- **Additive-only model change**: `'refunded'` appended to the `OrderStatus` union — no existing status renamed or removed.
- **Shared form over duplicated modals**: one `AddPaymentMethodForm` used by checkout and account prevents the "card popup doesn't sync with the full one" class of bug.
- **USD-only at the point of sale**: no KHR conversion shown anywhere in the PayWay flow; merchant fixed to "Nexora Co., Ltd"; price sits between merchant name and QR (reference-faithful layout).
- **Ledger is the wallet source of truth**: legacy wallet balance is derived/synced from completed ledger entries; `refund_credit` mirrors `top_up` mechanics.

